WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.322
A useful way to remember Pandas is as an eight-step workflow.

00:00:04.322 --> 00:00:13.837
We create or load a table, inspect it, select the rows and columns we need, clean quality problems, transform values,

00:00:13.837 --> 00:00:20.247
summarize the data, combine related tables, and finally validate the result.

00:00:20.247 --> 00:00:22.137
This order matters.

00:00:22.137 --> 00:00:29.232
For example, calculating revenue by category before checking whether the amount column is actually numeric can produce

00:00:29.232 --> 00:00:32.962
incorrect or unusable results.

00:00:32.962 --> 00:00:40.070
Similarly, joining two tables before understanding their keys can accidentally duplicate rows.

00:00:40.520 --> 00:00:43.972
Think of this workflow as a checklist you can reuse.

00:00:43.972 --> 00:00:50.645
Different projects may require different functions, but the reasoning process remains very similar.
